    "rejected": [
      "thm:residual-partition-minimality"
    ],
    "note": "Reject: the Bell(h) lower-bound construction is valid, but the Bell(h) upper bound is incompatible with the current residual definition using the same concrete complete-predecessor response-row suffix. Partition continuation proves equality of continuation support, not equality under a fixed global response table, which can distinguish numeric predecessor tuples forgotten by the partition. For h=1, two prefixes (1,0) and (1,1) have the same singleton partition but are separated by one common Y table mapping those tuples to 0 and 1 and the terminal atom Y_I=0. Define residuals modulo row renaming/abstract column support, or retain numeric histories; as written rho(h)=Bell(h) does not follow.",
    "at": "2026-09-13T16:26:18.895Z",
    "by": "adjudicator"
  },
